    "body": "Non-standard equipment requests are assessed on a case-by-case basis and subject to budget availability.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Software and System Access\n\n### 3.1 Standard Access (Provisioned Automatically)\nAll employees receive the following on their first day:\n- Company email (Microsoft 365)\n- Slack workspace\n- HR portal (leave, payroll, personal details)\n- Internal intranet and document management system\n- Video conferencing (Microsoft Teams)\n- Password manager (1Password)\n\n### 3.2 Role-Specific Access\nAccess to role-specific systems is provisioned based on the job role specified in the IT access request form. Common role-specific systems include:\n\n- **Developers/Engineers:** GitHub Enterprise, Azure DevOps, watsonx.ai, watsonx.orchestrate, cloud platform consoles (AWS/Azure/IBM Cloud)\n- **Analysts/Consultants:** Tableau, Power BI, watsonx.governance, data warehouse access\n- **Finance:** Xero, expense management platform\n- **Sales/Account Management:** Salesforce CRM\n\n### 3.3 Requesting Additional Access\nIf an employee requires access to a system not covered by their standard role provisioning, they must:\n1. Submit an access request via the IT portal\n2. Provide a business justification\n3. Obtain approval from their direct manager\n4."
